{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I woke up this morning with sharp pain near my G-tube, and it’s been constant. It goes around to my left side. Every time I tried to eat, I threw up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, chills, or changes in bowel movements?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or diarrhea. Just the pain and vomiting with food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Given your history of gastric bypass reversal and previous ulcers, we’re going to keep you NPO for now—nothing by mouth—to let your stomach rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no food at all? What about my tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll hold the tube feeds for now too. We’ll give you IV fluids to keep you hydrated and prevent low blood sugar, which we know you’re at risk for."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That makes sense. I’ve had this before—last time they helped me with Marinol for appetite."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll restart Marinol. We’ll also give you Zofran and Compazine for nausea. And we’ll vent your G-tube to relieve any pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I just hope it’s not another long stay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-10-09 23:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll take it day by day. Your labs look normal so far—no signs of infection or pancreatitis. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-10-10 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood work from last night is stable—normal white count, liver enzymes, lipase, and glucose. We’re going to keep you NPO today and recheck how you’re feeling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-10-10 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. The nausea is better since the Zofran. The pain is still there but not as bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-10-10 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s progress. We’ll keep managing the pain and nausea. We’re planning a CT scan today with contrast to make sure there’s no leak or blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-10-10 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had a CT a few months ago that showed inflammation near the anastomosis. Could that be it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-10-10 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s possible. But that scan didn’t show a leak. We’ll compare today’s to see if anything’s changed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-10-10 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CT came back. Good news—no signs of abscess, obstruction, or leak. The anastomosis looks normal, and your G-tube is in the right place."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-10-10 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why am I still in pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-10-10 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t have a clear answer yet. It could be related to inflammation or irritation from the tube. Since you’re not vomiting and labs are stable, we’ll try advancing your diet tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-10-10 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m willing to try. But slowly, please."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-10-11 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re going to start you on clear liquids. Small sips. If you tolerate it, we’ll move to full liquids later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-10-11 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’ve been craving something to drink. Will I still get the Marinol?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-10-11 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, twice a day. And we’ll keep your PPI and sucralfate to protect your stomach lining, especially since your last endoscopy showed ulcers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-10-11 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I had a few sips of apple juice and some broth. No nausea or pain so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-10-11 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’ll advance you to full liquids—yogurt, pudding, maybe some protein shakes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-10-11 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try a small meal later?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-10-11 12:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Let’s take it slow. We want to make sure you don’t relapse. Your blood sugar has been stable—staying in the 100s—which is great."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-10-12 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well yesterday. Today, we’ll try a soft, low-fat, low-sugar meal. Small portions. And we’ll clamp your G-tube to see how you do without venting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-10-12 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Should I still avoid tube feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-10-12 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For now, yes. Since you’re tolerating food, we’ll focus on oral intake. That’s actually the goal—getting you off tube feeds if possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-10-12 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I ate half a scrambled egg and some toast. Felt fine. No pain, no nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-10-12 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s fantastic. The nutritionist reviewed your intake and said you’re meeting over 75% of your calorie needs. That’s a big improvement."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-10-12 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been using the Dexcom like they told me. My sugars are staying steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-10-12 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s exactly what we want. You’re managing your hypoglycemia well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow. You’ve done really well—no pain, no vomiting, good oral intake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great! What meds will I go home with?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue all your home meds: fluoxetine, aripiprazole, gabapentin, atorvastatin, and the PPI. Also, sucralfate four times a day, Marinol twice a day, and Zofran as needed for nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give you a small amount of liquid oxycodone for breakthrough pain, but use it sparingly. Acetaminophen is safer for you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Should I restart tube feeds at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for now. Focus on small, frequent meals—low glycemic carbs, high protein. The dietitian will help you fine-tune this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have a follow-up with her next week. Should I wear the Dexcom all the time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. It helps catch lows before they become dangerous. Test your sugars before meals and at bedtime too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And if the pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2174-10-13 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your surgeon. If it’s severe or you start vomiting, come back to the ER. But I think you’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2174-10-13 18:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just got your CT report back. Confirms no acute issues—no leak, no obstruction. Everything looks stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2174-10-13 18:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it might be something serious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2174-10-13 18:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "So are we. Sometimes the pain is from irritation or inflammation that doesn’t show up on scans. But you’ve responded well to conservative care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home. We’ll send all your prescriptions to your pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel so much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did great. Keep up with your diet, meds, and follow-ups. Call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Have a good day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You too. The nurse will bring your discharge papers shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep the G-tube site clean and dry. Use the mupirocin ointment as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I remember from last time. I’ll take good care of it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2174-10-14 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m ready to go home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-10-09 23:08:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-10-14 17:35:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted for recurrent abdominal pain localized to her gastrostomy tube site, radiating to the left flank, with nausea and vomiting. She has a complex history including prior Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and reversal, post-surgical hypoglycemia, and gastrogastric anastomotic ulcers. Management was conservative: she was kept NPO initially, given IV fluids, and her G-tube was vented. Nausea was controlled with ondansetron and compazine, and pain was managed with acetaminophen and limited oxycodone. She gradually advanced to full liquids and tolerated oral intake well, with nutritional intake exceeding 75% of goal. A CT scan showed no acute intra-abdominal process, leak, or obstruction. Her blood glucose remained stable throughout. She was discharged home with instructions to continue PPI, sucralfate, Marinol, and ondansetron as needed, focus on small frequent meals, wear her Dexcom glucose monitor, and follow up with her dietitian and surgeon.",
    "problems": [
      "Epigastric pain",
      "Nausea with vomiting, unspecified",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Hypoglycemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
